<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    Address programming card — ALE settings pane (Mode settings → ALE), the
    app's fourth programming surface (plan-ale-programming.md §4.5, scope
    amendment X8). Built on the ModemPresetsView skeleton: Card border,
    CardHeading, DisabledReason caption, a two-tab strip with DataTrigger
    highlight, and a self-binding code-behind (DI singleton, loud-fail,
    Loaded → EnsureLoaded).

      "Program"       LEFT, DEFAULT — the kind segment row (Self/Individual/
                      Net/Member since round 15 E-1; labelled "Type" since
                      round 11 §3), then either the ADDRESS fields (Name, the
                      associated-self Picker, the channel-group ◀/▶ wheel) or,
                      under Member, the net and member Pickers and the picked
                      net's membership table — and ONE action button whose text
                      switches with the kind.
      "Address book"  RIGHT — every stored address of every kind, selfs
                      INCLUDED, each with a Delete behind a confirm that
                      re-arms on every press and, on NET rows, its membership
                      on a second line; the frameless ERASE button sits at the
                      bottom of THIS tab.

    Constitution notes:
    - NO blue ValueDisplay anywhere on this card (§4.5). An add-new form has no
      "current value" to read back: confirmed state renders ONLY as book rows.
      The ONE remaining ◀/▶ wheel display (channel group) is therefore a PLAIN
      cell-styled label, not the accent ValueDisplay border — it carries the
      operator's PENDING SELECTION, which is the recorded deviation from the
      Option-B rule (ui.md deviation ledger), and dressing that as a
      radio-state display is exactly what the rule forbids.
    - X5/K5: the entries are plain hint placeholders; the radio never writes
      an operator buffer, and nothing on this card prefills.
    - NO Refresh button (the round-9 doctrine): every editor landing re-reads
      the book, and the Address book tab is the lazy tier.
    - TWO-LEVEL gating (owner ruling 5): the whole card greys outside Ready +
      confirmed ALE, so landings and wheel spins still READ during a scan;
      the WRITE buttons additionally grey while scanning or while the radio is
      ON AIR (a call, a link, or an LQA - round 15 I-D2's one term), and the
      reason caption names the cause and the path.

    Wire notes: every write goes through the ONE programming gate and closes
    with a station-book re-read — the verify the operator sees. ADDM closes
    with the same read as the bracket's barrier and then re-reads the NET's own
    membership (round 11 §5 — the targeted `NETAD <name>` made that possible),
    so its verify is the member rows appearing, like every other write's.
-->
<ContentView xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:Falcon.App.Core.ViewModels;assembly=Falcon.App.Core"
             xmlns:behaviors="clr-namespace:Falcon.App.Behaviors"
             x:Class="Falcon.App.Views.SettingsParts.AleProgrammingView"
             x:DataType="vm:AleProgrammingViewModel">
    <ContentView.Resources>
        <!-- Row-local cell widths (rule K): the book rows and the member table
             are this card's own tables, so the widths live here rather than in
             App.xaml. (The WHEEL displays are different — round 11 §5 gave the
             three of them ONE shared key, AleWheelValueWidth.) -->
        <x:Double x:Key="AleWidthKind">44</x:Double>
        <x:Double x:Key="AleWidthName">120</x:Double>
        <x:Double x:Key="AleWidthGroup">36</x:Double>
        <x:Double x:Key="AleWidthMemberNumber">36</x:Double>

        <!-- The segment-row template (the SsbSettingsPaneView ChoiceButton,
             view-local copy). IsActive is the OPERATOR's pick: this is a
             compose-and-send surface, not a radio-state display. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="AleChoiceButton" x:DataType="vm:ChoiceItem">
            <!-- Round 10 §3: the kind buttons are the WIDE choice class
                 (SegmentWidthWide 90) — ONE ROW, label LEFT, inside the stated
                 phone budget (StyleVocabularyGuardTests pins the arithmetic,
                 reading the COUNT from the VM). ROUND 15 E-1 made it FOUR:
                 4 × 90 + 3 × 6 = 378 ≤ 394. -->
            <Button Text="{Binding Value}" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                    WidthRequest="{StaticResource SegmentWidthWide}"
                    Command="{Binding SelectCommand}"
                    SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding Value}">
                <Button.Triggers>
                    <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsActive}" Value="True">
                        <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                        <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                    </DataTrigger>
                </Button.Triggers>
            </Button>
        </DataTemplate>
    </ContentView.Resources>

    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}">
        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10">

            <Label Text="Address programming" Style="{StaticResource CardHeading}" />

            <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="{Binding DisabledReason}"
                   IsVisible="{Binding HasDisabledReason}" />

            <!-- Sub-tab strip: CARD-level, inside the card under the heading
                 (T3). Landing on Program re-reads the book (an editor
                 landing); the book tab reads only if nothing has loaded it
                 yet this session. -->
            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                <Button Text="Program" Style="{StaticResource Segment}" HorizontalOptions="Fill"
                        Command="{Binding OpenProgramTabCommand}"
                        SemanticProperties.Description="Program tab (add a self, individual or net address)">
                    <Button.Triggers>
                        <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsBookTabOpen}" Value="False">
                            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                        </DataTrigger>
                    </Button.Triggers>
                </Button>
                <Button Grid.Column="1" Text="Address book" Style="{StaticResource Segment}" HorizontalOptions="Fill"
                        Command="{Binding OpenBookTabCommand}"
                        SemanticProperties.Description="Address book tab (every stored address, with delete and erase)">
                    <Button.Triggers>
                        <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsBookTabOpen}" Value="True">
                            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                        </DataTrigger>
                    </Button.Triggers>
                </Button>
            </Grid>

            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsEnabled="{Binding AreControlsEnabled}">

                <!-- ========= Program tab ========= -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="True">
                    <VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>
                        <DataTrigger TargetType="VerticalStackLayout" Binding="{Binding IsBookTabOpen}" Value="True">
                            <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
                        </DataTrigger>
                    </VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>

                    <!-- Kind — ROUND 10 §3 (owner-final, 2026-08-16): the label
                         moves LEFT, joining every other row in the app; the
                         buttons stay RIGHT-aligned with the house 6-dp spacing
                         and take SegmentWidthWide. Switching kind is VIEW
                         STATE and sends NOTHING. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                        <!-- ROUND 11 §3: the label reads "Type". DISPLAY TEXT
                             ONLY — the VM property, the choices collection and
                             the wire are all still Kind. -->
                        <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Type" />
                        <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                               BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding KindChoices}"
                                               BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource AleChoiceButton}" />
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- Name: a HINT placeholder only (X5). Names are GLOBAL
                         across kinds — the radio refuses a duplicate and the
                         card shows its line; the app pre-checks nothing.
                         ROUND 15 E-1: hidden under Member, which programs a
                         RELATIONSHIP between two addresses that already
                         exist — there is no name to type. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6"
                          IsVisible="{Binding ShowAddressFields}">
                        <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Name" />
                        <!-- Round 10 §7: ONE bound for every kind. -->
                        <Entry Grid.Column="1" MaxLength="15"
                               Placeholder="1-15 characters"
                               Text="{Binding NameInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                               SemanticProperties.Description="Address name entry — sent trimmed and uppercased">
                            <Entry.Behaviors>
                                <behaviors:SelectAllOnFocusBehavior />
                            </Entry.Behaviors>
                        </Entry>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- Associated self — Individual and Net ONLY, and the
                         Self write path calls a TWO-argument wrapper, so a
                         stale selection can never ride along.
                         ROUND 15 E-5 (owner): the ◀/▶ wheel became a PICKER
                         and moved ABOVE the channel group, because picking the
                         self is what tells you which group to expect: the pick
                         SETS the group wheel to that self's group. It is a
                         DEFAULT, not a lock — the wheel still spins freely,
                         and the radio stores whatever group is sent. The offer
                         is the MIRROR's own selfs, in its listing order; an
                         empty book offers nothing to pick. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6"
                          IsVisible="{Binding ShowAssociatedSelf}">
                        <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Associated self" />
                        <Picker Grid.Column="1" Title="self"
                                ItemsSource="{Binding SelfChoices}"
                                SelectedItem="{Binding AssociatedSelfSelection, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                SemanticProperties.Description="Associated self to be programmed (view only — sends nothing)" />
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- Channel group — a ◀ display ▶ WHEEL over 0-9,
                         wrapping. The display carries the operator's PENDING
                         SELECTION (the recorded deviation); moving it sends
                         NOTHING. Chevrons are chevron-class 44 dp.
                         ROUND 15 E-5: the card's ONE remaining wheel. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6"
                          IsVisible="{Binding ShowAddressFields}">
                        <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Channel group" />
                        <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End">
                            <Button Text="◀" FontSize="10" Padding="0"
                                    WidthRequest="44" HeightRequest="44"
                                    Command="{Binding GroupDownCommand}"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="Previous channel group (view only — sends nothing)" />
                            <Label Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                   WidthRequest="{StaticResource AleWheelValueWidth}"
                                   FontFamily="Consolas" VerticalTextAlignment="Center"
                                   HorizontalTextAlignment="Center"
                                   Text="{Binding GroupText}"
                                   SemanticProperties.Description="Channel group to be programmed" />
                            <Button Text="▶" FontSize="10" Padding="0"
                                    WidthRequest="44" HeightRequest="44"
                                    Command="{Binding GroupUpCommand}"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="Next channel group (view only — sends nothing)" />
                        </HorizontalStackLayout>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- ROUND 11 §5 (owner ruling R2): the round-10 standing
                         two-line caption is DELETED and this CONTEXTUAL hint
                         replaces it — one line, on screen only while the
                         operator is composing a SELF longer than the three
                         characters the scan gate accepts. It states what the
                         radio does (stores) and what it will not do (satisfy
                         the gate), in operator words with no radio token in
                         them (R13). -->
                    <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                           IsVisible="{Binding ShowSelfGateHint}"
                           Text="{x:Static vm:AleProgrammingViewModel.SelfGateHint}" />

                    <!-- ===== Member: the two PICKERS (ROUND 15 E-1) =====
                         The Member kind adds an EXISTING address to an
                         EXISTING net, so both operands are picked from the
                         radio's own book rather than typed. Picking a net
                         reads that net's membership once per session — the
                         ONLY wire effect of any pick on this card. The member
                         offer is a property OF the net (individuals, plus
                         EXACTLY that net's own associated self — any other
                         self is refused), so it is empty and disabled until a
                         net is picked, and the caption says so. The offer is
                         FILTERED to the net's channel group (app policy
                         2026-08-23): a member in another group will not scan
                         with the net. The radio itself accepts a cross-group
                         member, so one added from the front panel still shows
                         in the membership table. Each candidate still shows its
                         group beside its name. -->
                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="{Binding ShowMemberSection}">
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                            <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Net" />
                            <Picker Grid.Column="1" Title="net"
                                    ItemsSource="{Binding NetChoices}"
                                    SelectedItem="{Binding NetPick, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="The net to add a member to" />
                        </Grid>

                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                            <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="Member" />
                            <Picker Grid.Column="1" Title="member"
                                    ItemsSource="{Binding MemberChoices}"
                                    ItemDisplayBinding="{Binding Display}"
                                    SelectedItem="{Binding MemberPick, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                    IsEnabled="{Binding CanPickMember}"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="The address to add, with its channel group" />
                        </Grid>

                        <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding ShowPickANetFirst}"
                               Text="{x:Static vm:AleProgrammingViewModel.PickANetFirstCaption}" />
                    </VerticalStackLayout>

                    <!-- ONE action button (ROUND 15 E-D2) — the whole address
                         as one command under the three address kinds, the
                         ADDM under Member, and the closing book read that
                         proves either. Round 10 §3: ACTION class, so the
                         SegmentWidth pin is DE-PINNED and the button sizes
                         naturally. Its TEXT switches with the kind, which is
                         exactly why it is ONE command seat and not two. -->
                    <Button Text="{Binding ActionText}" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                            HorizontalOptions="End"
                            Command="{Binding ActionCommand}"
                            SemanticProperties.Description="Program this address, or add this member to the net" />

                    <!-- ===== Net members (Member kind only) — ROUND 11 §5,
                         re-keyed by ROUND 15 E-1 =====
                         Membership became READABLE on 2026-08-17 (the targeted
                         `NETAD <name>` and its indented MEMBER nn lines), so
                         this section is a RADIO MIRROR: the picked net's rows
                         in the radio's own insertion order.
                         THREE STATES, never conflated: one hyphen row while
                         the net's membership is UNREAD, the caption when the
                         radio has CONFIRMED it empty, the rows otherwise.
                         There is NO Remove member: the wire has no such verb —
                         removal is the book tab's DELAD, which is global and
                         asks first — and the caption under the table says so
                         in prose rather than leaving the absence unexplained. -->
                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="{Binding ShowMemberSection}">
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                            <Label Text="#" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                   WidthRequest="{StaticResource AleWidthMemberNumber}" />
                            <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="Member" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}" />
                        </Grid>

                        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="6"
                                             BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding MemberDisplayRows}">
                            <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:AleMemberRow">
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                        <Label Text="{Binding NumberText}" FontFamily="Consolas"
                                               FontAttributes="Bold" FontSize="16"
                                               VerticalOptions="Center"
                                               WidthRequest="{StaticResource AleWidthMemberNumber}"
                                               SemanticProperties.Description="The radio's own member number" />
                                        <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding AddressText}" FontFamily="Consolas"
                                               FontAttributes="Bold" FontSize="16"
                                               VerticalOptions="Center"
                                               SemanticProperties.Description="Member address stored in this net" />
                                    </Grid>
                                </DataTemplate>
                            </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>

                        <!-- State 2 of three: the radio CONFIRMED this net has
                             no members (its own NO MEMBERS PRGMD). The unread
                             state is the hyphen ROW above, not this. -->
                        <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding HasNoMembers}"
                               Text="{x:Static vm:AleProgrammingViewModel.NoMembersCaption}" />

                        <!-- E-D1: the absence, stated. The radio has no
                             per-net removal verb, so the card offers none and
                             says what to do instead. -->
                        <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                               LineBreakMode="WordWrap"
                               Text="{x:Static vm:AleProgrammingViewModel.NoMemberRemovalCaption}" />
                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <!-- ========= Address book tab ========= -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="False">
                    <VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>
                        <DataTrigger TargetType="VerticalStackLayout" Binding="{Binding IsBookTabOpen}" Value="True">
                            <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="True" />
                        </DataTrigger>
                    </VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>

                    <!-- ROUND 11 §3: the column header reads "Type" (display
                         text only). §5/R3 added the PRIMARY column between the
                         associated self and the Delete: it is empty on every
                         row but the listing's FIRST SELF. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
                        <Label Text="Type" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                               WidthRequest="{StaticResource AleWidthKind}" />
                        <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="Name" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                               WidthRequest="{StaticResource AleWidthName}" />
                        <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="Grp" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                               WidthRequest="{StaticResource AleWidthGroup}" />
                        <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="Assoc self" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}" />
                    </Grid>

                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="6"
                                         BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding BookRows}">
                        <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:AleBookRow">
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*,Auto,Auto"
                                      RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                    <!-- ROUND 15 E-2: every row-0 cell is
                                         VERTICALLY CENTRED. The Delete button
                                         is 44 dp tall and the labels had no
                                         VerticalOptions at all, so the text
                                         sat at the top of the row and read as
                                         if it belonged to a different line
                                         than its own button. -->
                                    <Label Text="{Binding KindText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           VerticalOptions="Center"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource AleWidthKind}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Address kind" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding NameText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           VerticalOptions="Center"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource AleWidthName}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Stored address name" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding GroupText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           VerticalOptions="Center"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource AleWidthGroup}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Stored channel group" />
                                    <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="{Binding AssociatedSelfText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                           VerticalOptions="Center"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Associated self, or a dash when the radio reports none" />
                                    <!-- R3: the primary-self tag, on the book
                                         listing ONLY (the Operate selfs card is
                                         untouched). Position, not identity —
                                         it renders whichever self leads the
                                         radio's own listing. -->
                                    <Label Grid.Column="4" Text="{Binding PrimaryTagText}"
                                           Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                           VerticalOptions="Center"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding IsPrimarySelf}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="This is the radio's primary self" />
                                    <!-- ROUND 15 D: the NET row's member line,
                                         indented under Name and spanning
                                         Name·Grp·Assoc. It reads the SAME three
                                         states the Program tab's table does —
                                         the hyphen while unread, the read-empty
                                         caption, or the names in the radio's
                                         insertion order. It WRAPS rather than
                                         widening the row, so the 448-dp phone
                                         budget is untouched: the line lives
                                         inside the existing * column.
                                         Written BEFORE the Delete button so
                                         "Delete is the last cell" keeps holding
                                         literally (critic F36). -->
                                    <Label Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                                           Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                           Text="{Binding MembersText}"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding HasMembersText}"
                                           LineBreakMode="WordWrap"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Net members" />
                                    <Button Grid.Column="5" Text="Delete" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                            VerticalOptions="Center"
                                            Command="{Binding Delete}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding NameText}"
                                            SemanticProperties.Description="Delete this address from the radio" />
                                </Grid>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                    </VerticalStackLayout>

                    <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                           IsVisible="{Binding HasNoBookRows}"
                           Text="No addresses reported yet." />

                    <!-- ROUND 10 §5: the inline delete-confirm box is DELETED.
                         The question is a two-button POPUP (IConfirmationPrompt
                         — the VM never touches MAUI UI), raised on EVERY press,
                         and a SELF row's popup names the CASCADE. Its pins moved
                         with it, from markup to the VM's lifecycle tests. -->

                    <!-- ERASE — the guarded control, at the BOTTOM of the book
                         tab. ROUND 10 §5: the typed-token Entry is GONE from
                         here AND the token parameter is gone from Core; the
                         POPUP is the confirmation now, asked every press.
                         ROUND 15 E-3 (owner): the warn-stroked Border, the
                         SubHeading and the standing warning caption are
                         DELETED too. A frame and a paragraph that shout on
                         every landing are not what stops a mis-press — the
                         question is, and it is asked every time. What is left
                         is ONE button whose own text says what it does. -->
                    <Button Text="Erase address book" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                            HorizontalOptions="End"
                            Command="{Binding EraseCommand}"
                            SemanticProperties.Description="Erase every ALE address on the radio" />
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <!-- Notes, shared by both tabs: the client-side refusal, the
                     gate's outcome (empty on Accepted — the re-read row is the
                     proof), and why the write buttons are grey while the card
                     itself is live. -->
                <Label Style="{StaticResource ErrorCaption}" Text="{Binding InputError}"
                       IsVisible="{Binding HasInputError}" />
                <!-- ErrorCaption, deliberately: this is EMPTY on Accepted, so
                     the only things it ever renders are Refused / Unverified /
                     Failed — every one of them something the operator must
                     not miss on a programming surface. -->
                <Label Style="{StaticResource ErrorCaption}" Text="{Binding OperationStatus}"
                       IsVisible="{Binding HasOperationStatus}" />
                <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="{Binding WriteDisabledReason}"
                       IsVisible="{Binding HasWriteDisabledReason}" />
            </VerticalStackLayout>
        </VerticalStackLayout>
    </Border>
</ContentView>
